The British Independent Film Awards has announced the winners of their craft categories for 2026, with Clio Barnard's " I See Buildings Fall Like Lightning " leading the pack.

Having bowed to acclaim in Cannes, the feature &#x2014;&#xA0;following a group of lifelong friends grappling with pressures of life as they hit 30 &#x2014; landed three awards.

Shaheen Baig won for best casting, having previously won in 2022 for "Blue Jean," while best editing went to Maya Maffioli (nominated in 202 for "Rocks") and Connie Farr won her third best music supervision award after "All of Us Strangers" in 2023 and "Ali & Ava" in 2021. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories Steven Spielberg Calls ‘The Odyssey’ a ‘Showstopper’ and ‘One of the Greatest Things’ Matt Damon Has Ever Done Bruce Springsteen Says Steven Spielberg ‘F---ed Up’ Skinny Dipping After Releasing ‘Jaws’: ‘Why Would a Nice Man Do That?’

Meanwhile, dark period comedy "Savage House," won two awards, including best make-up and hair design for Jacquetta Levon (nominated in 2020 for "Saint Maud") and best costume design for Alex Bovaird.

The other BIFA craft awards were scattered across a number of titles, including "A Long Winter," "Ink," "Rose of Nevada," "Everybody Digs Bill Evans" and "The Magic Faraway Tree."

The rest of this year's BIFA winners &#x2014;&#xA0;including all the performance categories &#x2014;&#xA0;will be announced at the awards ceremony being held on Dec. 6.

