EXCLUSIVE: Netflix Brazil has set a release date for March of the Jaguars , the streamer&#x2019;s first wildlife documentary out of Latin America. The feature doc was created and produced in Brazil and is made by Alexandre Soullier and Emmanuel Priou, winner of the 2006 Oscar for Best Documentary Feature for March of the Penguins . Deadline has a first look at the trailer ahead of March of the Jaguars launching on Netflix globally on December 2

The film follows a family of jaguars at the Encontro das &#xC1;guas State Park in Brazil's Pantanal region. It has footage of the titular big cats that was captured over five years and 26 different expeditions. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article1-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid","mid-articleX","mid-article","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[2,2],[300,250],[620,350],[300,251],[501,282],[3,3],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories News Controversial "Netflix Tax" Could Raise Extra $2.1B For BBC By 2032, Research Finds Documentary Tyson Fury Reveals Schizophrenia Diagnosis In Netflix Doc

