Soullier and Priou produce alongside Mike Bueno and director Lawrence Wahba, who also co-wrote the screenplay with Fernanda Polacow.

&#x201C;In a way, my camera becomes the eyes of millions of people, revealing the wonders of nature in its rawest form, in remote and virtually inaccessible places,&#x201D; Wahba told Deadline.

&#x201C;In March of the Jaguars , we want to show jaguars as they have never been seen before, inspiring not only awe and wonder, but also an awareness of the urgent need to protect them. Bringing these images to audiences in more than 190 countries through Netflix is an extraordinary opportunity to turn wonder into awareness and, hopefully, awareness into action.&#x201D;

Jaguars are native to Brazil and it holds around half the world's wild population of the big cat. Wahba explained that jaguars have a special meaning for Brazilians and it was important to have a Brazilian team involved.

&#x201C;No one could tell this story quite like Brazilians can. To us, a jaguar is much more than just an animal. From a scientific perspective, it is a flagship species, a symbol of the conservation of entire ecosystems. In the cosmology of our Indigenous peoples, it is a sacred being, a messenger between the spiritual and physical worlds. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dl-mid-article-inject2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article2","mid-articleX","mid-article","mid","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

" March of the Jaguars balances scientific rigor with the poetic freedom to listen to and interpret the messages these extraordinary animals have to share with us.&#x201D;

